# .trivyignore - implements the dated waiver documented in docker/SECURITY.md
# ("Trivy scan waiver - 2026-08-27"). Every CVE below is explained there:
# why it isn't fixed yet, and what closing it actually requires.
#
# `exp:2026-09-27` matches SECURITY.md's own re-evaluation date - trivy stops
# honoring these entries after that date, so the CI gate goes back to
# enforcing 0 HIGH/CRITICAL until this file (and the waiver table) are
# updated against a fresh scan.
#
# A rebuild that changes any dependency version above must re-run the scan
# and update both this file and the SECURITY.md table, not assume the
# waiver still applies.

# OS package (liblcms2-2, base image - gcr.io/distroless/java-base-debian12)
CVE-2026-41254 exp:2026-09-27

# OS package (libexpat1, base image - gcr.io/distroless/java-base-debian12).
# Added 2026-09-02. Published after the 2026-08-27 waiver, which is why this file
# needed a second pass rather than being wrong originally: the CI gate went red on
# a branch that changed nothing in the image. Confirmed environmental, not a
# regression - re-running main's own last-green docker run (33534774002, commit
# f55a156) against the same day's Trivy DB reproduced the identical failure.
#
# Cannot be fixed by bumping the base digest: 2.5.0-1+deb12u3 carries the fix, but
# `gcr.io/distroless/java-base-debian12:nonroot` still resolves to the exact digest
# already pinned here (sha256:a9930cad...), i.e. Google has not published a rebuilt
# image yet. Re-check on the expiry date; if a newer digest exists by then, bump the
# pin in the Dockerfile instead of renewing this line.
CVE-2026-56408 exp:2026-09-27

# OS package (libexpat1, base image) - the SECOND libexpat CVE to land on this
# waiver, added 2026-09-11 during W6 D4. Same package, same base image, same
# reason as CVE-2026-56408 directly above, and re-confirmed rather than assumed:
#
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect gcr.io/distroless/java-base-debian12:nonroot
#     -> Digest: sha256:a9930cad62d02853d7f3dede7281c4b916cbf74493c2d8d38564121aad92bf6c
#
# That is the exact digest the Dockerfile already pins, so there is still no
# rebuilt base to move to; a local trivy scan of that base confirms it continues
# to ship 2.5.0-1+deb12u2 while Debian's fix is in 2.5.0-1+deb12u3.
#
# Not a W6 D4 regression: nothing in that deliverable touches the Dockerfile,
# netty, expat or Trivy config. main was last green on this scan on 2026-09-04
# and would fail identically if re-run today - the vulnerability database moved,
# the image did not.
#
# The CRITICAL that accompanied this one (CVE-2026-75595, netty-handler) was
# NOT waived - it was fixed properly by bumping ext['netty.version'] to
# 4.1.137.Final in build.gradle. A waiver is for what cannot be fixed today,
# not for what is merely inconvenient to fix.
CVE-2026-76957 exp:2026-09-27

